.\" man/man3/Docv::CLI.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::CLI" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::CLI \- The \fB\%docv\fR command: shows a manual page or a Markdown document in the viewer, or prints it as text when standard output is not a terminal.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBmodule Docv::CLI\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
The \fB\%docv\fR command: shows a manual page or a Markdown document in the
viewer, or prints it as text when standard output is not a terminal.
Without a page it opens the viewer on an empty page, the dock closed.
\fB\%path\-add\fR, \fB\%path\-rm\fR and \fB\%path\-list\fR manage the added man page
directories; \fB\%gen\-cr\fR generates the man pages of a Crystal shard.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBUSAGE\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
USAGE = "usage: docv [\-u]\en       docv [\-u] [section] name\en       docv [\-u] name(section)\en       docv [\-u] file          (a page, or a Markdown document: *.md ...)\en       docv path\-add dir...\en       docv path\-rm dir...\en       docv path\-list\en       docv gen\-cr [\-o dir] [shard]\en  \-u, \-\-unwrapped   start with unwrapped (one line per paragraph) layout\en                    (also [viewer] start\-wrapped = false in config.ini)\en  \-h, \-\-help        show this help\en\enWithout a page, the viewer opens on an empty page; p opens the dock with\enthe pages and documents of the current folder\(aqs project.\en\enPages are looked up in the man page directories of the project around\enthe current directory, then in the added directories, then along the\ensystem path (MANPATH, or man\-db\(aqs rules from PATH and man_db.conf).\enThe page search (/) also lists the project\(aqs Markdown documents; the\enproject\(aqs pages and documents come first.\en\en  path\-add dir...   add directories of man pages: trees (man1/, man3/...)\en                    or directories with pages in them\en  path\-rm dir...    remove added directories\en  path\-list         print the search path and where each entry comes from\en  gen\-cr            generate man pages of the Crystal shard at or above\en                    shard (default: the current directory) from README.md\en                    and its doc comments: name.7cr and Type.3cr pages in\en                    dir (default: man), relative to the shard root\en  text\-worker       (used by the viewer) read page paths from standard\en                    input and write the text of each page to standard\en                    output, for finding text across all pages\en\enConfiguration: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docv/config.ini (created on first run)\enAdded directories: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docv/paths"
.EE
.RE
.RE
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.PP
\fBdef self.run(args : Array(String)) : Int32\fR
